Swiss Ephemeris
  The installer downloads the Swiss Ephemeris data files (*.se1) from aloistr/swisseph and checks each one
  against its pinned commit. Source: https://www.astro.com/swisseph/swephinfo_e.htm.
  The licence page says Swiss Ephemeris "is made available by its authors under a dual licensing system"
  and that the developer "must choose between one of the two license models, which are a) GNU Affero General Public License (AGPL) b) Swiss Ephemeris Professional License". The timing clause reads:
  "The choice must be made before the software developer distributes software containing parts of Swiss Ephemeris to others, and before any public service using the developed software is activated."
  The AGPL option: "he or she must fulfill the conditions of that license, which includes the obligation
  to place his or her whole software project under the AGPL or a compatible license."
  The Professional option: "purchase the Swiss Ephemeris Professional Edition from Astrodienst and sign
  the corresponding license contract."
  On that wording, a public endpoint that runs this software can be a "public service using the developed
  software", so the choice applies before the endpoint is activated, not only before an image is published.
  Whether a given service is a public service is for the operator to decide.
