GeoNames
  The place lookup uses GeoNames data: cities500 (cities500.txt), admin1CodesASCII.txt and
  countryInfo.txt.
  Source: https://www.geonames.org/
  Licence: Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 (CC BY 4.0), https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/
  Credit: GeoNames asks for credit with a link or another reference to GeoNames when its data is used;
  the GeoNames export page is https://www.geonames.org/export/.
  The installer downloads these files into the data directory. This repository does not contain
  them. The committed sample data in data/fixtures is hand-written for tests and is not GeoNames data.
  The city list that Astrolog 8.00 installs, atlas.as, is composed from GeoNames data. Its header says:
  "Atlas composed May 14, 2026 using data from: https://www.geonames.org/" and "This work is licensed under a Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 License", and that Astrolog's processing and use of this data is still under Astrolog's GPL license.
